ommunist parties in the world and has played a crucial role in the political landscape of Greece and the broader Southern European region. Emerging from the turmoil of World War I and the subsequent social upheaval, KKE sought to establish a socialist society influenced by Marxist-Leninist principles. Key figures in its early years included Dimitris Giannopoulos and other intellectuals who were instrumental in defining the party's ideology and direction.

